{
  "Election": {
    "election_id": "th3pbp",
    "title": "BV2265 — Two-seat board by Bloc STAR: one more honest voter, and the council gets worse for them",
    "description": "The same six voters and the same two-seat board as the control election, plus a seventh voter whose honest ballot is Ada 3, Bruno 2, Cleo 5, Dov 0. Seat 1 is unchanged: Ada wins it. Seat 2 is not. The new voter's support lifts their favourite Cleo from 11 points to 16, which pushes Cleo past Bruno into the seat-2 runoff - and Dov beats Cleo there 4-2. So the council goes from Ada and Bruno to Ada and Dov: this voter traded a candidate they scored 2 for one they scored 0, and their own ballot rates the council they voted for (3 points) lower than the one they would have got by staying home (5). That is a participation failure, and the mechanism is specific to Bloc STAR: every seat rebuilds the finalist pair from whoever is left, with no reweighting to absorb support already spent. Nobody voted strategically and no tie-break was used. Full lesson & tabulation: https://masiarek.github.io/star-voting-library/02_STAR_Bloc/03_Criteria/participation/index.html",
